ankings tests and all 17 gallery tests passed. After the final label adjustment, all three rankings tests and the focused wheel test passed again. Coverage includes stable slice colours, outer-only selection, neutral focus, reduced motion and category placement.\n- Verified the running application shows no selection tick. Existing financial summaries are preserved; the snapshot comparison retains its three documented pre-existing funder data differences.\n\n![Rankings with style guide icons on desktop](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c2f0246-0c44-442b-af3f-094612a4716c)\n\n![Rankings with style guide icons on mobile](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec1c5a01-2e30-41b7-a955-4c94afa78c7d)","comments":[],"reviews":[],"title":"feat(rankings): add animated top-ten leaderboards","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/125"}
{"body":"## Why\n\nMP summaries need a declared amount for the current calendar year alongside the existing term and historical totals.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a backend-owned UTC calendar-year total and display the three totals in one row on desktop. Preserve the responsive layout below 1000px.\n- Show \"No declarations recorded\" for periods with zero declarations. Keep actual zero and unavailable amounts distinct.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Include every category registered within the current UTC year. Undated records remain historical only.\n- Preserve exact GBP decimals, counts, and existing term/history totals. Exclude known foreign currencies without conversion. Missing GBP amounts and unknown currencies still mark coverage incomplete.\n- Reuse the existing Metric component and declared-amount labels. No database changes.\n\n## Blast Radius\n\nThe member API and frontend gain two required fields and must deploy together. Funder calculations are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Rust calendar-year and HTTP fixture tests passed. Frontend check, production build, 39 parser/summary tests, and 34 browser tests passed. Required Clippy checks passed.\n- The three affected browser tests passed again after the desktop layout adjustment, including narrow-screen and empty-year checks.\n- Independent correctness and comment review found no actionable regressions. Updated desktop screenshots below use a test-supplied year to verify that labels follow the backend.\n- Snapshot comparison matched both MPs and all searches. Three funder differences also occur identically on unchanged main, so full production parity remains unverified.\n\n![Three declared totals aligned in one desktop row](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/24d6d66a-f550-484e-9527-8b16509b9f7d)\n\n![Single desktop row with no declarations recorded for the calendar year](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/570e1aaf-2607-42c3-8306-efd44dd78dc9)","comments":[],"reviews":[],"title":"feat(members): add calendar-year declared total","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/115"}
{"body":"A presentation change narrowed member headlines to employment and silently changed their totals. This restores declared GBP amounts across all categories and makes the backend the sole owner of both headline calculations.\n\nThe frontend requires the backend totals and coverage fields. It displays them without recalculation or fallback sums. AGENTS.md documents the category, currency, date, precision, missing-value and labeling rules, and requires an explicit user request for changes to financial meaning.\n\nOrdinary backend and frontend regression tests cover the calculation and display boundaries. The dedicated financial-contract workflow, frozen-baseline tooling and required GitHub check have been removed. A future verification skill is outside this PR.\n\nThe earnings chart keeps its employment scope. Source-record updates can change totals; presentation changes must preserve totals for fixed records. Deploy the backend before the frontend if released separately. Legacy SQLx test queries now name the schema explicitly so they compile against a fresh database.\n\nPreviously verified against development data and the running application: Nigel Farage's two headlines show £2,323,720.45. The production calculation and display code are unchanged by the CI simplification.\n\n![Desktop summary on the rebased branch](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0b6d8568-2870-4056-84be-29eef2f65361)\n\nValidation after simplification: all nine backend entity-details tests passed, Svelte checks reported zero errors and warnings, and the full Clippy pre-commit hook passed. The seven relocated backend expectations and SQL records were compared with the originals and match exactly. Independent review found no blockers.","comments":[],"reviews":[],"title":"fix(totals): centralize declared amounts and document financial rules","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/103"}
