[{"body":"## What changed\n\nResolution now uses the cleaner's extracted aliases in both candidate generation and match acceptance. For explicitly typed trade unions, whole-token `Unite` evidence brings differently written branch names into the same candidate set. HSBC executive-title variants can link when their distinctive name terms and normalized numbered-street addresses agree. Source names and payment occurrences remain intact; the canonical display name uses the most reported source spelling.\n\nThe rules keep ambiguity visible: similarly spelled entities without the required evidence remain separate. A clean-to-resolve CLI regression test verifies that Carlton Club and Carlton Club Political Committee, despite sharing an address, remain separate and are emitted for review.\n\nA run against the available cleaned declarations grouped all 7 HSBC observations as one identity and all 103 explicitly typed Unite trade-union observations as one identity, while keeping Carlton Club separate from its committee.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p exposed --lib` — 72 passed\n- `cargo test -p exposed --test declaration_resolution_cli -- --ignored --nocapture` — passed with real Splink\n- `python -m unittest discover -s resolution/tests -v` — 6 passed\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n\nStrict Clippy still reports existing lint failures in unrelated loading code.\n","number":27,"title":"Use extracted evidence in funder resolution","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/27"},{"body":"## Why\n\nMP summaries need a declared amount for the current calendar year alongside the existing term and historical totals.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a backend-owned UTC calendar-year total and display the three totals in one row on desktop. Preserve the responsive layout below 1000px.\n- Show \"No declarations recorded\" for periods with zero declarations. Keep actual zero and unavailable amounts distinct.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Include every category registered within the current