t, combine the registration-week label with its heading, and remove the peak amount label above it.\n- Remove declaration and funding count blocks, currency sections, and the counted history link.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe member summary and shared member declaration amounts change. The weekly graph groups declarations by registration week because payment dates are unavailable. The API contract and funder page retain their existing behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Frontend check and production build pass. The initial 34 Playwright tests pass. The three member summary browser tests pass after the disclosure and chart layout updates.\n- The live Nigel Farage total is £2,323,720.45. All 112 weekly values match an independent Decimal calculation, including 30 weeks with recorded earnings.\n- The desktop screenshot uses the running branch with live API data. The peak label is absent and the plot fills its former space.\n\n![Desktop member summary](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e736011f-6ddb-4904-bb3c-05b29a7ca197)","number":50,"title":"feat(frontend): add weekly earnings to member summaries","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/50"},{"body":"A presentation change narrowed member headlines to employment and silently changed their totals. This restores declared GBP amounts across all categories and makes the backend the sole owner of both headline calculations.\n\nThe frontend requires the backend totals and coverage fields. It displays them without recalculation or fallback sums. AGENTS.md documents the category, currency, date, precision, missing-value and labeling rules, and requires an explicit user request for changes to financial meaning.\n\nOrdinary backend and frontend regression tests cover the calculation and display boundaries. The dedicated financial-contract workflow, frozen-baseline tooling and required GitHub check have been removed. A future verification skill is outside this PR.\n\nThe earnings chart keeps its employment scope. Source-record updates can change totals; presentation changes must preserve totals for fixed records. Deploy the backend before the frontend if released separately. Legacy SQLx test queries now name the schema explicitly so they compile against a fresh database.\n\nPreviously verified against development data and the running application: Nigel Farage's two headlines show £2,323,720.45. The production calculation and display code are unchanged by the CI simplification.\n\n![Desktop summary on the rebased branch](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0b6d8568-2870-4056-84be-29eef2f65361)\n\nValidation after simplification: all nine backend entity-details tests passed, Svelte checks reported zero errors and warnings, and the full Clippy pre-commit hook passed. The seven relocated backend expectations and SQL records were compared with the originals and match exactly. Independent review found no blockers.","number":103,"title":"fix(totals): centralize declared amounts and document financial rules","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/103"},{"body":"## Why\n\nAdd the three requested current-term charts to the home page. Reuse the authoritative member summaries so every view uses the same declared GBP rules.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add quartile ranges, the top five MPs, and a party pie chart through a server-rendered overview.\n- Preserve exact decimal amounts, declaration counts, unknown values, and partial totals.\n- Add a wrapping party legend and tests for its shared component contract.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Current Commons MPs, with declarations registered on or after 9 July 2024 across every category.\n- Known GBP amounts only, without currency conversion. Undated records stay outside the current term.\n- Rank groups exclude unavailable amounts. Partial known amounts remain labelled. Parties use latest recorded affiliation.\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\nA single database snapshot reuses the existing domain summarizer rather than duplicating financial rules in SQL. Four rank groups show exact minimum and maximum amounts, with member ID breaking ties.\n\n## Blast Radius\n\nThe home page now requests the overview from the server and retains its navigation when data is unavailable. Existing member totals and the default party legend layout remain unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Rust entity-details tests passed, 16 tests including PostgreSQL and live HTTP. The commit hook passed frontend checking and strict Clippy across all targets and features.\n- Frontend check and production build passed. All 49 unit tests and 28 affected browser tests passed.\n- Built homepage verified against the imported database with 650 MPs and 17 parties, exact amounts, JavaScript disabled, and desktop and mobile widths. Desktop screenshot attached.\n\n![Desktop home page with current-term declaration charts](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d6e1ea8-1132-4bd2-980e-034a51f9329c)","number":119,"title":"feat(home): add current-term declaration charts","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/119"},{"body":"## Why\n\nReplace the MP registration-month earnings chart with a ranked source table that works without a colour legend.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Link each funder beside its exact declared GBP amount.\n- Reuse existing unavailable-amount wording and flag incomplete values.\n- Keep the table to the requested source data. Remove per-source entry counts and explanatory copy.\n\n- Give every shared table a divider above its first data row, including when column headings are visually hidden.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Group sources across all historical categories and dates, including undated records.\n- Preserve backend headline totals, declaration counts, dates, category totals and calendar-year totals.\n- Preserve decimal precision, negative amounts, zero and null. Exclude known foreign currencies without conversion or incompleteness. Missing GBP amounts and unknown currencies keep source values incomplete.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Divider regressions fail before the shared CSS fix with expected `1px`, received `0px`. After the fix, 51 gallery and entity-detail browser tests pass. Both source and declaration dividers measure `1px solid`.\n\n- `npm run check`, `npm run build` and the 36 affected entity-detail browser tests pass. Independent copy and correctness review passes.\n- Desktop and mobile screenshots use the running branch build with exact local snapshot data. Links, keyboard scrolling, unavailable amounts and partial known amounts are covered.\n- The earlier full comparison matched all searches and both MPs. BBC, GB News and Premier League have identical snapshot-versus-production differences on unchanged main. This copy correction does not change financial calculations.\n\n![MP source table with the shared first-row divider on desktop](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/88e1d9cf-59b9-4bb7-a53b-671a9737aec1)\n\n![MP source table with the shared first-row divider on mobile](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e233f4ce-defb-404c-b290-79d1b42765d1)","number":117,"title":"feat(members): replace monthly earnings with declared money sources","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/117"},{"body":"## Why\n\nMP readers need historical, parliamentary-term and calendar-year declared amounts together below the name and metadata.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the two headline metrics with a three-row table. The historical label includes the earliest known registration month and year.\n- Add mandatory backend calendar-year metadata and totals, with a typed UTC year and the existing exact GBP aggregate.\n- Preserve distinct empty, unavailable and zero states. Incomplete amounts retain a hover tooltip; totals have no helper text beneath them. Totals retain the original responsive font size, weight and colour. Long amounts support keyboard scrolling.\n\n## Scope\n\n- All categories participate, including unknown category IDs. Historical totals include every record; term totals retain the inclusive 9 July 2024 UTC boundary.\n- The new annual total includes registrations in the backend-selected UTC calendar year. Undated records remain historical only.\n- Exact decimal GBP values, counts and nulls remain intact. Known foreign currencies are excluded without marking totals incomplete; unknown currencies and missing GBP amounts do mark them incomplete. There is no currency conversion or browser recalculation. Labels describe declared amounts.\n\n## Blast Radius\n\nThe MP API gains mandatory year fields, so the backend and frontend must update together. Funder aggregation and stored data are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Frontend check and build passed. All 68 affected Playwright tests passed, including table order, UTC labels, precision and keyboard overflow.\n- Targeted Rust service and HTTP contract tests passed against PostgreSQL. Rust check, formatting and the full pre-commit Clippy check passed.\n- Snapshot comparison matched both selected MPs and all searches. Three funder differences produced exit 1; unchanged main reproduced identical observations and differences. Both isolated runs cleaned up successfully.\n\nScreenshots use fixture data, including a deliberately different backend year to verify that the label follows the supplied total.\n\n![MP declared totals on desktop](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d6cb56b-0a3a-48f7-b016-8a25803a4cfe)\n\n![MP declared totals on a narrow screen](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/76b41c24-48e9-4810-b12a-b0e57cf3df69)","number":113,"title":"feat(members): show declared totals in a period table","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/113"},{"body":"## Why\nRename the MP source summary to \"Top amount\" and show the five highest ranked sources.\n\n## What changed\n- Limit the displayed source table to five rows using the existing exact-amount ranking.\n- Update browser coverage to verify the heading and exclusion of a sixth source.\n\n## Scope\n- MP summary pr…10956 tokens truncated…three independent reviews. Strict workspace Clippy for all targets and features, and formatting, passed.\n- Real read-only HTTP checks passed for search, funder details, and one event per failed request. The server also served requests and logged failures once with its default stderr sink. GET and HEAD database failures returned generic and empty bodies while causes appeared only in logs. The serializer privacy regression failed before the fix and passes afterward. An injected duplicate event made the count test fail with 2 versus 1; the probe was removed.\n- The frozen search regression is blocked by its missing `funder_group_names` table, tracked in #82. The snapshot was left unchanged. A supplemental run against current development data matched four cases and differed on Unite search results.\n\n\n","number":83,"title":"feat(tracing): trace backend adapter operations and failures","url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/83"}]
